WEBVTT

00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:02.600
Let me introduce...

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:03.960
This is my childhood friend,

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:05.930
Nagisa Shiranami.

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:08.320
Your childhood friend...

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:09.560
Is a guy?

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:11.330
Hiyori, they are?

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.030
They are...

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.430
Nice to meet you, I'm Someya.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:18.530
I'm Shibasaki.

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:22.630
He's huge!

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.160
LIP×LIP?

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:26.200
Do you know them?

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.800
A lot of girls like to scream when they read magazines.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.730
They are celebrities, aren't they?

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.130
Why are you with them?

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:35.900
Um, they are my classmates.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.360
We're just classmates.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:42.100
If they're just classmates, why are they here with you?

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:44.060
That's because...

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:46.760
You always change the topic

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:48.460
whenever I ask about your part-time job.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:50.030
It has something to do with them, right?

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:53.000
You can't lie to me.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:59.500
Actually, I'm their trainee manager.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:01.100
Manager?

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:02.700
Just a trainee, okay?

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:26.660
Heroine Tarumono!
The Unpopular Girl and the Secret Job

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:41.930
Hiyori.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:44.330
You've changed.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:49.930
What do you mean by that?

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:51.560
Is it strange?

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.630
Did I become cute?

00:02:57.430 --> 00:02:58.160
Yes.

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:00.600
Yes! That's great!

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:02.400
I dressed up

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:03.760
just to give you a surprise.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:05.200
For me?

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:07.960
You said it when we were young, right?

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:09.430
That dresses don't fit me.

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:15.160
So, I got them to become my producers.

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:22.430
Her childhood friend seems to like her.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:25.160
It seems like that, but we can't be sure yet.

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:28.230
That said, she didn't tell us Nagisa is a guy.

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:30.700
I thought it's a girl.

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:34.660
That girl left out the most important information.

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:36.900
There's still time before the concert.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.500
Is there anywhere you want to go?

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:40.700
Your workplace.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.130
Why?

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:45.900
I want to see where you work.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.500
All right, I'm going to tell President Tamura we're here.

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:51.000
Please wait here.

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:52.100
Okay.

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:58.360
You made your classmate your manager.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.230
What are you thinking?

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:02.500
She's the one who wanted to do it.

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:04.760
Otherwise, she would have given up a long time ago.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:06.730
Even if she doesn't like it,

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:09.700
Hiyori will never give up once she's decided on something.

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:11.260
She's that kind of person.

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:16.160
Hiyoko is really cute!

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:17.830
That outfit really suits you.

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:20.500
Thank you.

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:23.430
It's thanks to them being my producers.

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:24.930
You're idols

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.700
but you chose to become producers for your manager.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.330
Instructing a girl on how to dress up...

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:31.760
Don't you think that's too much?

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.960
What an intense reaction. Are you jealous?

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.500
You like Suzumi, right?

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:39.660
This has nothing to do with you.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.700
Acting as producers for our manager

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:47.260
is not something we usually do.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:51.300
But that's because she looks too unfashionable.

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:52.230
Right?

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:55.230
She looks so bad that it's embarrassing
to walk with her on the streets.

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:59.100
She lacks the grace and charm a woman should have.

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:01.130
She doesn't look like a girl at all.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:03.700
And she wants to become a heroine.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:05.960
There should be a limit to being naive.

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:08.530
We only helped her a bit,

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:11.200
it's impossible for anyone to fall for her.

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:13.530
You agree as well, right?

00:05:14.130 --> 00:05:16.260
As a girl, she's too plain.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:18.530
Hiyori is a good girl.

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:20.560
But that's her only redeeming quality.

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:22.000
That's not it!

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:23.600
Even if you're childhood friends,

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:25.000
you don't have to protect her that much.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:27.700
To be honest, there's no reason for you to choose
Suzumi as your girlfriend, right?

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:29.460
There is!

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:31.900
She's my only choice!

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:37.030
Okay, it's confirmed.

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:39.630
You like Suzumi, don't you?

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:46.500
I'm sorry for messing with you.

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:49.330
We only wanted to know your true feelings.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:52.760
Even if my opponents are idols,

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:54.860
I will never give up on Hiyori.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:56.100
What?

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:58.000
I will never give her up!

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:01.360
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:03.300
The president will be here soon.

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:05.360
What happened?

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:07.200
It's nothing.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:13.330
Thanks for taking care of Hiyori all this while.

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:16.080
(IWAMI SPECIALTY: DRIED PUFFERFISH)
This is our local delicacy.

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:18.860
Ah, thank you.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.700
Please try it.

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:24.200
Though Tokyo has many delicious foods,

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:26.230
we won't lose on taste as well.

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:28.060
I look forward to it.

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:29.230
Please.

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:30.400
Nagisa-kun!

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:33.760
Are you interested in showbiz?

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:36.300
You have good looks and style.

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:37.530
The crowds will love you.

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:40.160
I think you can become an excellent idol.

00:06:41.030 --> 00:06:42.430
Thank you for your offer

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:45.660
but I've decided to inherit my family business.

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:46.700
Family business?

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:50.330
Nagisa's family runs a famous restaurant.

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:52.430
My father is a fisherman.

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:53.860
He supplies his catch to Nagisa's shop.

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:56.500
Our parents are always busy,

00:06:57.030 --> 00:07:00.530
so we always played together when we were young, right?

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:01.700
That's right.

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:03.760
After I take over the shop,

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:06.730
I will make it even more popular.

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:08.960
That's my dream.

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:11.260
That's a great dream.

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:13.560
What a shame.

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:18.460
Where will you be staying today?

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:20.060
A business hotel.

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:22.200
You can stay at my place, you know?

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:25.860
How can I do that?

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:26.900
Why?

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:28.260
You're asking why?

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:31.130
That's because I've made a reservation.

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:34.730
You're acting too distant.

00:07:34.730 --> 00:07:36.930
You could have saved some money.

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:39.860
She didn't realize it at all.

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:41.460
She's too slow.

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:07.830
FT4 members are all masters in their fields.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:10.660
The one who gathers all these talented members

00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:12.230
is their leader, IV-san.

00:08:12.230 --> 00:08:14.800
He's in charge of everything in FT4.

00:08:15.330 --> 00:08:17.000
He may be standing at the back,

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:20.030
but he's the core pillar that supports FT4.

00:08:27.760 --> 00:08:30.000
You're brilliant! You're the best!

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:32.960
Everyone! Are you excited?

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:34.200
Yeah!

00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:36.160
The atmosphere is great.

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:37.760
But not as great as me.

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:42.300
DAI's "not as great as me" has appeared!

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:44.100
Next, let's quiet down a bit.

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:47.230
We have a big announcement!

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:50.060
- What is it?
- Hurry and announce it!

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:52.430
Hey, who should announce it?

00:08:52.730 --> 00:08:54.230
It's me, of course.

00:08:54.330 --> 00:08:55.930
No, it's me.

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:57.900
Though I wanted to say that.

00:08:58.630 --> 00:09:00.000
But let's do it together!

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:01.800
Full Throttle 4!

00:09:02.230 --> 00:09:04.760
Best Artist Countdown Live!

00:09:04.760 --> 00:09:06.180
Participation confirmed!

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:09.000
Congratulation!

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:15.200
We're able to enter it all thanks to you!

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:17.400
Yeah! It's awesome!

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:19.760
We're awesome after all.

00:09:19.860 --> 00:09:21.000
That's right.

00:09:21.230 --> 00:09:23.230
We will continue to work hard and move forward!

00:09:23.230 --> 00:09:24.560
Please join us!

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:26.330
We will!

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:34.660
FT4's songs and performance are awesome!

00:09:34.930 --> 00:09:37.800
Their members trust each other as well.

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:40.960
Yeah, trust is important, right?

00:09:41.460 --> 00:09:44.760
Those two have great teamwork at crucial times as well.

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:47.260
Those two... Are you talking about LIP×LIP?

00:09:47.430 --> 00:09:50.330
Yeah, they should trust each other

00:09:50.330 --> 00:09:53.230
but instead, they always fight. It's really troubling.

00:09:56.350 --> 00:09:57.300
Good job.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:10:00.360
What's with the long face? Did you fight again?

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:02.430
How could we fight?

00:10:02.860 --> 00:10:05.560
FT4 had announced their participation
in the Best Artist Countdown Live.

00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:08.160
We have to go back to the office. See you.

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:13.200
They've become motivated.

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:16.300
It's right to bring them to the FT4 concert.

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:16.980
Hey,

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:19.700
you're hungry, right?

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:24.300
It's the first time I see you cook.

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:26.160
But aren't you tired?

00:10:26.460 --> 00:10:27.360
No way.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:30.060
I brought my cooking utensils just for this.

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:31.760
You brought them here?

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:35.760
A long time ago, when I was bullied

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:38.660
because my family owns a restaurant, you would say,

00:10:39.460 --> 00:10:43.000
"The food at Nagisa's restaurant tastes the best!"

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:46.160
Did I say that?

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:47.900
You did.

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:49.730
That's why I've always wanted

00:10:50.200 --> 00:10:53.100
to cook something delicious for you.

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:55.860
I see. I look forward to it.

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:04.600
Oh, specialized kitchen knives!

00:11:05.530 --> 00:11:06.560
That's amazing!

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:08.060
Just like a real chef!

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:14.460
All right! It's done.

00:11:16.060 --> 00:11:17.400
It looks so healthy!

00:11:20.520 --> 00:11:22.260
Thank you for the food.

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:24.200
They taste great!

00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:25.900
Thank goodness.

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:28.400
I wanted to cheer you with it.

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:31.560
I heard you failed to get into the preliminary.

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:33.700
I thought you will be depressed.

00:11:34.230 --> 00:11:35.600
But thankfully, you look fine.

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:38.130
I was depressed for a time

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:40.060
but I've recovered.

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:41.860
This is thanks to LIP×LIP.

00:11:43.330 --> 00:11:46.330
Back then, I thought little about idols.

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:49.100
But after I saw their concert,

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:51.100
I felt really inspired.

00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:54.400
That's a rosette I've obtained from them.

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:55.860
It's something I treasure very much.

00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:59.330
Though they have bad personalities,

00:11:59.330 --> 00:12:01.370
they have gentle sides as well.

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:04.630
They even become my producer...

00:12:04.630 --> 00:12:05.500
At that time,

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:09.000
at my aunt's wedding,

00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:11.330
I told you the dress didn't fit you because

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:14.560
when you're wearing that dress, you're...

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:17.060
You're too cute.

00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:21.330
I don't want anyone to take you away from me, so I...

00:12:26.500 --> 00:12:27.300
I...

00:12:31.160 --> 00:12:32.530
I like you, Hiyori.

00:12:40.260 --> 00:12:42.360
Um, I'm sorry for saying that all of a sudden.

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:44.060
Did I scare you?

00:12:46.860 --> 00:12:48.030
I should go now.

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:49.660
You don't have to answer me yet.

00:12:50.130 --> 00:12:52.130
You can call or message me.

00:12:52.660 --> 00:12:53.860
Thank you for today.

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:57.660
I will take the Shinkansen back tomorrow.

00:12:57.930 --> 00:12:59.730
See you.

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:05.730
Um...

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:07.730
What just happened?

00:13:11.030 --> 00:13:12.400
Was it a confession?

00:13:13.260 --> 00:13:17.460
No way!

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:29.730
Hiyoko? Hiyoko?

00:13:30.980 --> 00:13:31.720
Yes!

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:34.830
Are you all right? You look tired.

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:38.230
Sorry. I didn't sleep well last night.

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:39.630
Is that so?

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:42.030
There's nothing urgent today.

00:13:42.030 --> 00:13:43.230
You can go back first.

00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:44.530
But...

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:46.960
You should rest when you need it.

00:13:46.960 --> 00:13:48.100
It's important as well.

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:49.200
Do you understand?

00:13:49.330 --> 00:13:51.160
Yes, I'm sorry.

00:13:57.900 --> 00:13:59.100
Good job, guys.

00:13:59.630 --> 00:14:00.400
Phew.

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:01.430
Good job.

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:11.000
Did Nagisa confess?

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:14.460
How did you know?

00:14:14.800 --> 00:14:17.600
It's clear that he likes you.

00:14:18.300 --> 00:14:20.430
I wasn't aware of it!

00:14:20.430 --> 00:14:21.730
You're very slow at realizing it.

00:14:23.430 --> 00:14:24.930
What should I do?

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:27.100
You should follow your own heart.

00:14:27.100 --> 00:14:29.930
I don't know what I should do!

00:14:32.230 --> 00:14:35.060
He will make a good boyfriend, won't he?

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:37.560
That's right. He's not a bad choice.

00:14:37.830 --> 00:14:41.260
Good looks, good personality, good family background.

00:14:41.530 --> 00:14:43.400
He's an ideal prince, isn't he?

00:14:43.730 --> 00:14:45.530
Prince?

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:47.630
You wanted to become a heroine, right?

00:14:48.100 --> 00:14:51.960
Don't you want to live happily ever after with the prince?

00:14:55.630 --> 00:14:57.930
If I can become a heroine just like that,

00:14:57.930 --> 00:14:59.330
I will be willing.

00:15:00.300 --> 00:15:01.230
But...

00:15:05.530 --> 00:15:06.700
Please save me!

00:15:11.500 --> 00:15:14.130
Suddenly saying "Please save me!" like that is so funny!

00:15:14.360 --> 00:15:16.560
It's not something to laugh at.

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:19.030
Sorry for calling you out.

00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:20.400
It's completely okay.

00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:22.800
I kind of welcome it, right?

00:15:24.300 --> 00:15:25.660
We're friends after all.

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:28.600
Thank you.

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:31.260
Nagisa looks like a model.

00:15:31.730 --> 00:15:32.530
A handsome man.

00:15:33.730 --> 00:15:35.630
Juri-chan, you have a boyfriend, right?

00:15:36.130 --> 00:15:38.600
Yeah. We're in a lovey-dovey relationship.

00:15:39.130 --> 00:15:41.660
I'm oblivious to love.

00:15:41.760 --> 00:15:43.460
When did you realize you love him?

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:47.100
When was it?

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:51.700
He's a waiter at the café I frequent.

00:15:52.100 --> 00:15:55.160
At first, I thought he is very approachable and friendly.

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:57.360
He's completely not my type,

00:15:58.160 --> 00:16:00.400
but after talking to him so many times...

00:16:00.900 --> 00:16:02.060
Somehow,

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:05.530
it became "he's nice" and "I think I like him".

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:09.300
Now, I think he's the most handsome man in the world

00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:10.630
and completely my type!

00:16:10.930 --> 00:16:12.830
That feels like love!

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:15.100
Love is great.

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:18.300
If you don't understand, you can try dating him a bit.

00:16:18.400 --> 00:16:20.800
Um... but...

00:16:22.100 --> 00:16:24.130
It's a confession by your childhood friend!

00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:26.460
You should accept it! Definitely!

00:16:26.560 --> 00:16:27.500
Why?

00:16:27.600 --> 00:16:29.100
A handsome childhood friend...

00:16:29.100 --> 00:16:31.130
Do you know how many girls adore this setting?

00:16:31.130 --> 00:16:33.030
A confession by your childhood friend...

00:16:33.030 --> 00:16:34.330
"I've always liked you!"

00:16:34.330 --> 00:16:36.030
Do you know how many people dream about

00:16:36.030 --> 00:16:37.130
experiencing this situation?

00:16:37.130 --> 00:16:38.560
You can never reject it!

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:39.630
Really?

00:16:39.630 --> 00:16:40.600
Yes.

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:42.360
A handsome childhood friend confessing to you is just like

00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:43.560
getting rescued by your Prince Charming!

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:45.230
Isn't this just like a heroine?

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:47.130
That's too cliche, right?

00:16:47.930 --> 00:16:49.330
What's wrong with cliches?

00:16:49.760 --> 00:16:52.260
Cliches are good. No, cliches are the best!

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:54.500
Suzumi-san, do you know how lucky you are?

00:16:54.500 --> 00:16:55.960
How dare you get troubled by this?

00:16:57.860 --> 00:16:58.660
It's unfair.

00:17:00.100 --> 00:17:02.660
Calm down, Chizuru.

00:17:07.230 --> 00:17:08.100
I'm sorry.

00:17:09.660 --> 00:17:12.900
Can we still be friends after a confession?

00:17:13.660 --> 00:17:16.960
I grew up with Nagisa. He's like family.

00:17:17.560 --> 00:17:19.930
I don't want this to change.

00:17:20.800 --> 00:17:22.530
Maybe Nagisa has the same feeling.

00:17:23.760 --> 00:17:26.300
It's best if his confession works.

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:29.430
But if it fails, what should he do?

00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:32.630
I think he feels uneasy as well.

00:17:34.830 --> 00:17:37.860
He must have gathered a lot of courage to confess to you.

00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:41.760
Hiyori, you should tell him your true feelings.

00:17:43.100 --> 00:17:45.460
My true feelings...

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:51.480
ALL CALLS

00:17:51.480 --> 00:17:53.930
JR LINE RAILWAY

00:17:53.930 --> 00:17:55.260
Nagisa!

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:10.660
Hiyori.

00:18:12.600 --> 00:18:13.400
I'm sorry.

00:18:15.030 --> 00:18:16.860
I can't date you right now.

00:18:20.930 --> 00:18:22.530
Do you have someone you like?

00:18:25.060 --> 00:18:26.660
Is he from LIP×LIP?

00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:31.060
No, no. That's not it!

00:18:31.060 --> 00:18:33.430
I'm just their trainee manager.

00:18:33.430 --> 00:18:35.560
It has nothing to do with that!

00:18:35.830 --> 00:18:37.500
But, you said you're inspired.

00:18:37.500 --> 00:18:39.060
But that's their song

00:18:39.060 --> 00:18:40.560
and stage performance.

00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:43.460
It's just like how you get motivated by FT4.

00:18:43.900 --> 00:18:45.730
So, why?

00:18:46.330 --> 00:18:49.230
I think I'm happy with my life at the moment.

00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:52.560
In school, tracks, or as a trainee manager.

00:18:52.700 --> 00:18:55.300
I can do my best in everything.

00:18:55.900 --> 00:18:57.530
Though there are hard times,

00:18:57.600 --> 00:18:59.060
they are important to me.

00:18:59.300 --> 00:19:01.860
I've never thought about

00:19:01.860 --> 00:19:03.100
giving up any of them.

00:19:04.730 --> 00:19:07.530
I want to do my best until the very end.

00:19:07.900 --> 00:19:10.030
So, what should I say...

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:13.800
You won't think about love at the moment, right?

00:19:16.700 --> 00:19:17.430
Yeah.

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:26.560
What are you doing?

00:19:29.360 --> 00:19:31.400
You look cute when you're dressed up.

00:19:32.130 --> 00:19:35.730
But you look cute when you're running, too.

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:39.500
I was too impatient.

00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:41.330
I'm sorry for troubling you.

00:19:43.060 --> 00:19:46.330
Um, I've something to tell you, too.

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:48.460
Not through the phone or message,

00:19:48.460 --> 00:19:49.560
but I want to tell you in person.

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:52.430
Thank you for your confession!

00:19:54.600 --> 00:19:57.060
Though it shocked me, I was really happy.

00:19:57.660 --> 00:19:58.530
Really?

00:19:58.830 --> 00:19:59.500
Yeah.

00:19:59.500 --> 00:20:04.130
That's because I thought no one will ever confess to me.

00:20:04.330 --> 00:20:05.960
But now I'm confident

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:08.300
that I can also become a heroine.

00:20:08.960 --> 00:20:10.500
You are a heroine.

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:12.900
It's always been true for me.

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:18.630
What's that?

00:20:18.630 --> 00:20:20.130
That's too embarrassing.

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:22.640
Yeah.

00:20:25.560 --> 00:20:28.600
I will come to Tokyo once I graduated from high school.

00:20:30.560 --> 00:20:33.230
I don't think it's enough to just inherit the shop.

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:36.460
I want to study management at university

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:38.330
and train in a restaurant here.

00:20:39.560 --> 00:20:40.660
I will work hard as well.

00:20:41.330 --> 00:20:43.930
So, we will meet again.

00:20:45.060 --> 00:20:45.830
Yes.

00:20:52.630 --> 00:20:54.830
Nagisa, see you!

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:05.630
Hiyoko, please help me with this!

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:07.830
Okay!

00:21:10.300 --> 00:21:11.230
What's wrong?

00:21:11.460 --> 00:21:12.860
You've turned back to your old self.

00:21:13.230 --> 00:21:15.100
Why did you change back?

00:21:16.700 --> 00:21:18.660
I've experienced being stylish thanks to you two.

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:20.400
I was really happy

00:21:20.400 --> 00:21:22.700
but dresses are not suitable for running.

00:21:22.830 --> 00:21:24.230
What kind of excuse is that?

00:21:24.930 --> 00:21:27.030
Don't you want to be a heroine anymore?

00:21:27.100 --> 00:21:28.730
Of course.

00:21:28.730 --> 00:21:30.860
In between tracks and being a manager,

00:21:30.860 --> 00:21:32.960
I want to become a confident heroine as well.

00:21:33.230 --> 00:21:35.760
Then, no one will confess to you.

00:21:35.760 --> 00:21:36.800
It might be your last chance

00:21:36.800 --> 00:21:38.730
to become a heroine.

00:21:39.260 --> 00:21:40.730
That's not true!

00:21:40.730 --> 00:21:42.430
As long as I work hard...

00:21:42.430 --> 00:21:44.360
All right, work hard then.

00:21:44.600 --> 00:21:46.560
I hope that your efforts will bear results.

00:21:46.800 --> 00:21:50.930
Seriously, stop making fun of me!

00:21:51.010 --> 00:21:55.020
Episode 7 My Childhood Friend

